Skip the NAND bad-block-table scan in the Rockchip NFC driver so probe succeeds
on a chip whose existing content was written by the vendor rknand FTL (mainline
ECC can't decode it -> the BBT scan marks blocks bad and BBT creation fails with
-ENOSPC, aborting probe). With the scan skipped, /dev/mtd0 is created so the chip
can be inspected. Set the flag right before nand_scan(): this driver installs
controller.ops (with .attach_chip) after the per-chip nand_scan() call, so setting
it in attach_chip runs too late / not at all.

--- a/drivers/mtd/nand/raw/rockchip-nand-controller.c
+++ b/drivers/mtd/nand/raw/rockchip-nand-controller.c
@@ rk_nfc_nand_chip_init(), just before nand_scan() @@
 	mtd_set_ooblayout(mtd, &rk_nfc_ooblayout_ops);
 	rk_nfc_hw_init(nfc);
+	/* s3plus: vendor rknand pages fail mainline ECC; skip the bad-block table
+	 * scan/write so probe succeeds and /dev/mtd is created for raw dump. */
+	chip->options |= NAND_SKIP_BBTSCAN;
 	ret = nand_scan(chip, nsels);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
